<title>UK: Spain sets 1.25 billion euro Eurobond due Jan 2008.</title>
<headline>Spain sets 1.25 billion euro Eurobond due Jan 2008.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Banco Central Hispano, Paribas, Santander de Negocios and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SPAIN</p>
<p> AMT   1.25 BLN EURO  COUPON     6.00	MATURITY    31.JAN.08</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    31.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	**TO BE PRICED LATER</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    SPANISH   HOME CTRY  SPAIN     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND APR.07 ECU OAT / APR.22 ECU OAT</p>
<p> NOTES	OBLIGATIONS PAID/RECEIVED IN ECU UNTIL EMU WHEN IT</p>
<p>		WILL BE FUNGIBLE WITH OUTSTANDING BONO ISSUE.</p>
<p>		SHORT FIRST COUPON.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
